On 2007-10-12, Kernigh <xkernigh@netscape.net> wrote:
> If logging works great with ToME, would it work great with NetHack or
> SLASH'EM? Perhaps I should read Ellora first, to learn how to do this.

Logging your character seems to be a way to force yourself to pay
attention to what you're doing in-game, so that you remember what you're
doing in-game _and_ you remember things that worked for you.

If you're willing to spoil yourself, then keep the spoilers handy so you
can easily reference them.  I wouldn't think that logging would be
_necessary_, but if you tend to just bang keys and try to plow through
over and over, then it might be a way to slow your play down and cause
you to focus more.

I definitely wouldn't use Ellora as a good example, though.

> I have never ascended, and in only one game (in view of
> nethack.alt.org) did I reach Juiblex. Perhaps if I logged more
> characters, then I might reach Juiblex more often.

NetHack isn't really much of an RPG, and logging seems to be an
artificial way to force RPG-like elements into it for the benefit of the
player's mind.  If that's the _only_ way to focus for you, go for it;
but I would suggest just slowing down the physical speed of your play, 
using ; when you see new monsters appear and you don't know instantly
what they are and all ramifications, etc.

Also, you probably want to just plain run away more often.

